  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. Here N≤60N \\le 60N≤60. This is worth 100100100 points in Division 111 and unscoreable elsewhere.**\n\nYou are given integers NNN and DDD, please count the number of pairs (X,Y)(X, Y)(X,Y) satisfying the following conditions:\n\n\n1≤X&lt;Y&lt;2N1 \\le X &lt; Y &lt; 2^N1≤X&lt;Y&lt;2N\nY−X=DY - X = DY−X=D\ngcd⁡(X,Y)=X⊕Y\\gcd(X, Y) = X \\oplus Ygcd(X,Y)=X⊕Y \\\\\nHere, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the Bitwise XOR operator.\nSince the answer may be large, output it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input contains 222 integers - NNN and DDD.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of pairs (X,Y)(X, Y)(X,Y) satisfying the conditions modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤602 \\le N \\le 602≤N≤60",
      "1≤D≤min⁡(2N−2,2000)1 \\le D \\le \\min(2^N - 2, 2000)1≤D≤min(2N−2,2000)",
      "The sum of DDD over all test cases does not exceed 200020002000."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6\n3 2\n4 1\n4 14\n7 5\n10 20\n60 1800",
        "output": "1\n7\n0\n6\n13\n401643732",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The only pair satisfying all constraints is (4,6)(4, 6)(4,6). We can verify gcd⁡(4,6)=2=4⊕6\\gcd(4, 6) = 2 = 4 \\oplus 6gcd(4,6)=2=4⊕6.\nTest Case 2 : The pairs satisfying the conditions are (2,3)(2, 3)(2,3), (4,5)(4, 5)(4,5), (6,7)(6, 7)(6,7), (8,9)(8, 9)(8,9), (10,11)(10, 11)(10,11), (12,13)(12, 13)(12,13) and (14,15)(14, 15)(14,15)."
      }
    ]
  },
